WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:05.120
Although Unreal Engine has many uses in film simulations

2
00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.540
and real-time experiences, it's always fundamentally

3
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.140
been a game engine.

4
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.580
It allows users to create content,

5
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.619
then allow players to interact with it

6
00:00:13.619 --> 00:00:16.500
and influence that content.

7
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.019
While there are many benefits to using Unreal Engine,

8
00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.859
for the purposes of this course,

9
00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:22.219
we're going to focus primarily

10
00:00:22.219 --> 00:00:25.059
on the features and tools that directly relate

11
00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:27.179
to video game development.

12
00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:29.179
Small disclaimer, this slide does not actually

13
00:00:29.219 --> 00:00:31.859
show the complete pipeline used in video games.

14
00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:34.500
Rather, it's designed to help you understand that making video

15
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:38.140
games is an intricate and heavily interconnected process.

16
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.899
Most video games today made will

17
00:00:39.899 --> 00:00:43.140
experience some kind of development, release,

18
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:46.380
patching, and possibly additional content release

19
00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.899
through updates, patches, or DLC.

20
00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:51.579
When it comes to developing your cutscenes pipeline,

21
00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:54.200
the hope is that you will build systems and frameworks,

22
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.380
as well as your file and folder structures,

23
00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.560
that allows you to reduce iteration times,

24
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.200
avoid asset dependency breakages,

25
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.759
and build a flexible framework that

26
00:01:02.759 --> 00:01:07.239
will connect the player character, NPCs, world assets,

27
00:01:07.239 --> 00:01:10.040
and your cinematic experiences.
